      "summary": "Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Skip to content Home Episodes Episode 4: العمارة كالبُعد المفقود في التحول Episode 4 العمارة كالبُعد المفقود في التحول 2026-01-28T02:48:31.019Z Hosted by Dr. Darren Pulsipher Explore more in the episode archive . Summary Digital transformation continues to struggle—not because organizations lack technology, but because they misunderstand the real impediments to change. In this episode of Digital Transformation Architect, Dr. Darren Pulsipher revisits the foundational constraints of desirability, feasibility, and viability and explains why they still shape success or failure today. Rather than chasing tools or trends, this episode focuses on how strategy, architecture, technology, and people must come together as a coherent system. Drawing from real-world experience across AI, cybersecurity, data, edge, and modern infrastructure, Dr. Pulsipher challenges leaders to rethink how transformation is designed, governed, and sustained. This conversation cuts through hype to show why enduring transformation requires intentional system design—and why architecture remains the missing link between vision and execution. Darren W Pulsipher Digital transformation continues to struggle—not because organizations lack technology, but because they misunderstand the real impediments to change. In this episode of Digital Transformation Architect, Dr. Darren Pulsipher revisits the foundational constraints of desirability, feasibility, and viability and explains why they still shape success or failure today.",
